 res←execUserCode(event ns eventargs);stack;prefix;async;exec;fn;expr;cmd;niladic;varname;larg;x;ok;haslarg;call
⍝ Run user callback code
 varname←'#.EWC._ARGS_',⍕⎕TID
 expr←1⊃event
 haslarg←1<≢event
 larg←{⊃⍣(1=≢⍵)⊢⍵}1↓event
 ⍎varname,'←larg eventargs'

 async←'&'=¯1↑expr
 niladic←exec←'⍎'=1↑expr
 fn←exec↓(-async)↓expr
 :If ~(⊂'∆DQ')∊⎕SI ⍝ Switching to calling space won't automatically put us in the right namespace
     fn←(⍕ns),'.',(exec/'('),fn,exec/')'
 :EndIf

 res←⍬
 :If exec
     'W'Log 'NB ⍎callbacks not properly supported - expression executed BEFORE default processing'
 :ElseIf 3≠ns.⎕NC fn
     'E'Log'Callback function not found: ',fn
     →0
 :Else ⍝ It's a function
     niladic←0=1 2⊃ns.⎕AT fn ⍝ Niladic fn
 :EndIf

 ⍝ Build the callback expr, ⎕IO-independently (it runs under the app's ⎕IO, may be 0).
 ⍝ As native ⎕WC (checked on 20.0): a registration extra ('fn' data) is the LEFT
 ⍝ arg if fn takes one - dyadic or ambivalent; a monadic fn gets just the event
 ⍝ message, the extra dropped; a niladic fn gets nothing.
 :If niladic
     expr←fn ⋄ call←'Niladic'
 :ElseIf haslarg∧2=|1 2⊃ns.⎕AT fn  ⍝ dyadic (2) or ambivalent (¯2) callback: extra is the left arg
     expr←'(⊃',varname,')',fn,' ⊃1↓',varname ⋄ call←'Dyadic'
 :Else  ⍝ monadic callback, with or without an extra
     expr←fn,' ⊃1↓',varname ⋄ call←'Monadic'
 :EndIf
 'P'Log'    ',call,' call to ',1⊃event

 x←(⎕RSI∊⎕THIS)⍳0 ⍝ How far up the stack to go to escape EWC
 :If async
    res←⍬ ⊣ x 0 (86⌶)&expr
 :Else
    :Trap 11
        (ok res)←x 0(86⌶)expr
    :Else
        :If 'Invalid left argument'≡⎕DMX.Message
        :AndIf 'execUserCode'≡12↑2⊃⎕DMX.DM
            res←x(86⌶)expr ⍝ Don't have the extension from svn revision 51229
        :EndIf
    :EndTrap
 :EndIf
